ation_ms":3,"error_message":"Memory at 1,259/1,375 chars. Adding this entry (403 chars) would exceed the limit. Consolidate now: use 'replace' to merge overlapping entries into shorter ones or 'remove' stale or less important entries (see current_entries below), then retry this add — all in this turn.","is_error":true,"result_preview":"{\"success\": false, \"error\": \"Memory at 1,259/1,375 chars. Adding this entry (403 chars) would exceed the limit. Consolidate now: use 'replace' to merge overlapping entries into shorter ones or 'remove' stale or less important entries (see current_entries below), then retry this add — all in this turn.\", \"current_entries\": [\"Prefers using the `mcp-router` MCP tool (via MCP Router app) for external service queries like Redmine, rather than attempting local CLI commands or generic web searches.\", \"EXO cluster: Two Macs on 192.168.88.x — mini M4 32GB at 10.1.2.7, pro M3 Pro 18GB at 10.1.1.9. Source: /Volumes/AI/exo/ (v0.3.70, mDNS auto-discovery, no RDMA — no TB cable). Apps: dev build at /Volumes/AI/exo/app/EXO/build/Build/Products/Release/EXO.app v1.0.1 (preferred); public at /Applications/EXO.app v1.0.69. Plist ~/Library/Preferences/exolabs.EXO.plist, key `EXOStaticPeers` in format `/ip4/<ip>/tcp/52415` (leading slash required). Swift wrapper sets `EXO_BOOTSTRAP_PEERS` env var (logs som...","status":"error","task_id":"1462c4b0-7e66-4b20-a54e-d2acad180599","tool_call_id":"call_function_j8nxbe9a08n0_1","tool_name":"memory","turn_id":"20260701_040209_4ee2de:1462c4b0-7e66-4b20-a54e-d2acad180599:cff8ec49"},"sessionId":"20260701_040209_4ee2de","timestamp":"2026-07-01T19:36:24.660577+00:00"},"type":"raw"}}␀␀␀��␀<S��